==Battleground==
*1 [[Loris]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*8 [[Relic Doge]]s (100%) spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Relic Doge]] (1%) spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Cyberhorn]]s spawn, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
**3 [[LeMurr]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s (100%) spawn, delay 30~40 seconds<sup>900f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[Loris|Lorises]] spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
If acquired by this point, [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] will prove extremely useful, due to the level only containing Alien and Relic enemies. [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] are able to easily hold off the LeMurrs and their crushing DPS. However, take care that the former does not get cursed by Loris.

The general strategy is simple: you will want to kill the Cyberhorns as fast as possible, both giving you a large sum of money and allowing you to damage the LeMurrs that would otherwise hide behind them. Alternatively, you can use the limited peon count at the start to stack [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cats]], preventing the enemies from pushing at all.

If the Lemurrs become too much of a problem in later difficulties, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat's]] [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]] should make quick work of them.

